## The ancient spaceport, the spaceship and where it lands.

## Room 13. LOOK.BAS 1300 and 1350.

create the Observatory
  a room
  room name:
    Observatory
  exits, one-way: east to the Waiting Room, out to the Waiting Room

  This was an observatory for the people of the ancient cities.

## Room 14. LOOK.BAS 1400 and 1450.

create the Spaceship
  a room
  room name:
    Spaceship
  states, reversible: on-first-planet, at-port, on-planet
  exits, one-way: in to the Strange Planet
  out to the Strange Planet, one-way while not the Spaceship is at-port

  passage to the Strange Planet
    grammar
      door
    while the Spaceship is on-planet
  end passage

  You are in spaceship lit by red and blue lights on it's{br}
  sides. The spaceship's manual controls are damaged.

## Room 29. LOOK.BAS 2900 and 2950.

create the Control Room
  a room, dark while not lit-up
  room name:
    Control room
  exits, one-way: west to the Waiting Room, southeast to the Junction of Tunnels

  This room was once the control room for an ancient spaceport.{br}
  There are cspace maps, tracking devices, and other{br}
  intricate devices on the walls.

## Room 30. LOOK.BAS 3000 and 3050.

create the Waiting Room
  a room, dark while not lit-up
  room name:
    Waiting room
  exits, one-way: north to the Observatory, northeast to the Control Room, in to the Waiting Room
  west to the Launching Area, one-way while not the Spaceship is at-port

  This was a waiting room for passengers on spaceships.{br}
  There are doors to the north,west,and NE.

## Room 31. LOOK.BAS 3100 and 3150.

create the Launching Area
  a room, dark while not lit-up
  room name:
    Launching area
  exits, one-way: east to the Waiting Room, out to the Waiting Room

  You are on a launching area for spaceships.

## Room 32. LOOK.BAS 3200 and 3250.

create the Strange Planet
  a room, dark while not lit-up
  room name:
    Strange planet
  in to the Spaceship, one-way while not the Spaceship is at-port

  You are on a building on some strange planet. A door goes out.
